diff --git a/crates/team-control-plane/README.md b/crates/team-control-plane/README.md
index b6b9be8..179e5b3 100644
--- a/crates/team-control-plane/README.md
+++ b/crates/team-control-plane/README.md
@@ -225,3 +225,68 @@ Takeover securely classifies retained raw `.log` files without a size limit or
 whole-file allocation. Native JSON receipts and bootstrap `.info` metadata retain
 the 1 MiB bound; unsafe files, incomplete inventory and active work still refuse
 transfer.
+
+
+## Exact admitted v2 contracts
+
+`POST /v2/contracts/commands` accepts strict schema2 JSON with `key`,
+`expected_revision`, `recovery_epoch`, `task` and a tagged `command`.
+`GET /v2/contracts/tasks/{task}` authenticates the same bearer and returns
+canonical source snapshots, full WorkRef, immutable Intent/Acceptance/Plan
+identities, current revisions, dependency dispositions and accepted subjects.
+WorkRef namespaces include ledger, deployment, tenant, project and immutable item.
+The broker retains source bytes, their SHA256 and exact source revision; source
+availability is an explicit admitted input. A `source.propose` event retains an
+inert proposal and cannot change admitted work or satisfy a dependency.
+
+`intent.admit`, `plan.admit` and `dependency.revalidate` require Owner authority
+unless an Owner has explicitly admitted `delegation.admit` for the exact work,
+mission, current lead principal and RoleEpoch, permitted command families and
+effects, cumulative intent/plan ceilings, resource ceilings and expiry. The
+transaction rechecks authentication, current role and delegation on replay.
+Delegated intent amendments preserve every current exact prerequisite, including
+suspended and explicitly revalidated bindings. Removing or replacing prerequisites
+requires explicit Owner amendment or the admitted proof revalidation seam.
+Intent changes and declarative strategy changes have separate immutable IDs.
+Plans have a known schema/interpreter version, stable step IDs, explicit DAG
+edges/joins, effect allowlists, finite loops and repair/resource ceilings.
+Plan replacement preserves completed steps and cannot increase a previously
+admitted ceiling. This API stores and validates plans; ticket29 owns execution.
+
+Dependencies bind exact prerequisite WorkRef, IntentRevision, accepted subject
+and policy. Broker admission of a superseding prerequisite suspends fresh
+Attempt/Worker Episode/workspace/gateway-operation grants. It retains previous
+operation receipts and reconciliation. Revalidation requires a new current exact
+accepted subject; reading or replaying an old receipt cannot reopen admission.
+A Ready Worker allocation cannot acquire a fresh EpisodeGateway Start receipt
+after suspension; an earlier persisted Start remains inspectable and reconcilable.
+
+Production has a separate exact proof seam. An authenticated independent verifier
+uses `verification.bind` before its Episode has an allocated execution, pinning
+IntentRevision, AcceptanceContract, policy and environment. The task must already
+require supervised verification and its ArtifactService policy must match.
+`production.verify` then checks the actual ArtifactService candidate/report and
+independent trusted monitor measurements against that binding. Owner or a
+bounded current delegated lead uses `outcome.accept`. Existing v1 candidate and
+verification formats and IDs remain intact; an old v1 PASS or acceptance alone
+cannot acquire a v2 binding.
+Fresh legacy ArtifactService Accept refuses mapped work. Unmapped v1 acceptance
+and exact historical accepted receipts retain their identities without writing
+a fresh v2 accepted outcome.
+
+Workers may use `outcome.propose` to retain immutable evidence. A contract that
+expressly allows negative research can use separate `research.verify` and
+`outcome.accept` commands to recognize `investigation_complete`. The verifier
+must differ from the proposer; evidence remains referenced through normal
+ArtifactService collection. Evaluator-change proposals remain unpromoted and
+cannot satisfy this contract. Workers cannot verify or accept their proposals.
+Attempt cancellation fences v2 outcome proposals, verifier bindings, proofs and
+acceptance, including exact command replay. Authenticated snapshots, retained
+evidence, historical outcomes and earlier effect reconciliation remain available;
+cancellation does not implicitly refund capacity or cumulative admission counts.
+
+Migration0008 is additive. Legacy specifications and original nullable
+Role/Episode/Attempt provenance stay unchanged; legacy mappings remain explicitly
+closed for v2 until exact Owner admission. Migration never upgrades a v1 proof or
+invents an original Attempt. Durable scopes, Kata API/event qualification, Plan
+interpretation and v0.2 assembled recovery remain later tickets.
